    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Bryson Stott** (70.86) anchor our lineup as the highest-projected options. **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive park boost and a favorable matchup against the left-handed Lopez, while **Bryson Stott** is a priority play due to a significant platoon advantage and a slow opposing delivery that screams potential for a stolen base, a critical metric for our roster. Similarly, **Brendan Donovan** (67.39) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.65) offer elite efficiency, with **Brendan Donovan** taking advantage of a high-ceiling platoon spot and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining a must-start regardless of the marginal SP_xERA concern given his projected output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Wenceel Perez** (52.86). While he carries a strong platoon edge against the southpaw, his projected efficiency fell just short of the threshold required to displace our current starters. We are keeping a close watch on **Will Smith** (43.14), who faces a dangerous Chris Sale; his score is suppressed by the matchup, but he retains his spot as we await final confirmation of the batting order. The lineup is further bolstered by **Cal Raleigh** (61.58) and **Gavin Sheets** (59.46), both of whom are positioned well to capitalize on their respective matchups. \n\nRisks today center largely on the high volume of \"Lineup Pending\" designations. We have assumed aggressive placement for **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee**, all of whom see their value fluctuate significantly based on their spots in the order. Furthermore, while **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** receive a slight bump from wind-out conditions, we remain cautious about the impact of facing Carmen Mlodzinski, whose expected ERA suggests a tighter window for production than the raw wind-assisted projections imply. Keep an eye on final lineup cards to ensure our assumed order holds, as any shift down the lineup could trigger a re-evaluation of the bench.",
